<HelpChapterSection Id="news">
    <HelpTopicSection Id="news-read">
        <p>Open <span class="help-ui">News</span> in the menu.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Category tabs: <span class="help-ui">All</span>, “News”, “Announcement”, “Event”, “Training and development”, “Projects and achievements”.</li>
            <li>The <span class="help-ui">Search news</span> field searches titles and summaries.</li>
            <li>Cards show the cover image, category, the <span class="help-ui">Pinned</span> badge, title, summary, date, the author with a photo and the numbers of views, reactions and comments. Pinned posts always come first, then from newest to oldest.</li>
            <li>There are 9 cards per page; the number can be changed (9, 18, 36, 72).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Click a card to open the post: category, date, number of views, cover image, author, summary and full text. Photos in the text and in galleries open full screen: browse with the arrow keys, the buttons or a swipe, close with <kbd>Esc</kbd>. The <span class="help-ui">All news</span> button returns to the feed. The latest news is also shown on the home page.</p>
        <p>A view is counted once per reader. If a post has been deleted or unpublished — “News post not found”.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="news-discussion">
        <p>Reactions and comments are below the text of a post. New comments and reactions of other readers appear without reloading the page.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Reactions.</strong> Click <span class="help-ui">React</span> (the smiley with a plus) and choose an emotion: 👍 Like, 👎 Dislike, ❤️ Love, 👏 Applause, 🎉 Congratulations, 😄 Funny, 😮 Wow, 🤔 Doubtful, 😢 Sad, 😡 Outrageous. Each reader has one reaction per post: another emotion replaces the previous one, clicking your own again removes it. Comments can be reacted to the same way.</li>
            <li><strong>Comment.</strong> Type in the “Write a comment…” field (up to 2,000 characters) and click <span class="help-ui">Send</span>. The newest comments are on top; <span class="help-ui">Earlier comments</span> loads older ones.</li>
            <li><strong>Reply.</strong> <span class="help-ui">Reply</span> under a comment opens a reply field. Replies are collected under the comment in one level; a reply to a reply goes into the same thread and addresses the person by name.</li>
            <li><strong>Your comment</strong> can be edited with <span class="help-ui">Edit</span> (it gets an “(edited)” mark) or deleted with <span class="help-ui">Delete</span>. If someone has already replied, “The comment was deleted.” stays in its place so the thread holds together.</li>
            <li><strong>Moderation.</strong> News editors of the organization the post belongs to can delete any comment under it; such deletions are recorded in the audit log (“Comment deleted”).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Only published posts can be commented on. If the editor has turned comments off, the post shows “Comments on this post are turned off.” — reactions still work.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="news-list">
        <p>In the news feed, click <span class="help-ui">Manage</span> (or <span class="help-ui">Administration</span> → <span class="help-ui">News</span>). Here you see the posts of the organizations whose news you manage (an administrator of all organizations sees all of them), including drafts — only editors can see them.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Search — by title or summary.</li>
            <li>Columns: <strong>Title</strong> (and category), <strong>Status</strong> (“Draft” / “Published”, “Pinned”), <strong>Published</strong>, <strong>Modified</strong>, <strong>Organization</strong> (“Entire cabinet” — for general news), <strong>Author</strong>, the <span class="help-ui">Edit</span> button.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">New post</span> — create a news post.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="news-editor">
        <ol class="help-steps">
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">New post</span> (in the feed or on the management page) or <span class="help-ui">Edit</span> next to an existing one.</li>
            <li>Fill in the <span class="help-ui">Title</span> (up to 200 characters) and <span class="help-ui">Summary</span> (up to 500 characters, 1–2 sentences for the card).</li>
            <li>Write the <span class="help-ui">Text</span> in the visual editor (up to 50,000 characters) — headings, lists, tables, photos and galleries, see “<a href="/help#news-formatting">Text formatting, photos and galleries</a>”.</li>
            <li>In the “Publication” card, choose the <span class="help-ui">Organization</span> the post belongs to: the communications specialists of that organization will be able to edit it. The <span class="help-ui">Entire cabinet (all organizations)</span> option is available only to an administrator of all organizations. Published news is read by employees of all organizations, and the post's card shows its organization.</li>
            <li>Choose a <span class="help-ui">Category</span>. The <span class="help-ui">Published</span> checkbox makes the post visible to everyone (it is checked for a new post; uncheck it to save a draft). <span class="help-ui">Pin to top</span> — the post will always be first. <span class="help-ui">Allow comments</span> (on) — readers can comment; reactions are always available.</li>
            <li>Optionally add a cover image: <span class="help-ui">Choose an image</span> — JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF or GIF up to 15 MB, preferably with a 16:9 aspect ratio (it is compressed to AVIF). To remove the current cover image, check <span class="help-ui">Remove cover image</span>.</li>
            <li>Click <span class="help-ui">Save</span> — “Post saved”. For a published post, the <span class="help-ui">View</span> button opens it the way readers see it.</li>
        </ol>
        <ul>
            <li>The post's address is generated from the title when it is created and never changes, so links to the post don't “break” after editing.</li>
            <li>If you unpublish a post and publish it again, the original publication date is kept.</li>
            <li><span class="help-ui">Delete</span> (for an existing post) — after the “Delete the post permanently?” confirmation, the post is deleted forever together with its photos, comments and reactions. To just hide a post, uncheck “Published”.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Possible errors: “Enter a title.”, “Enter a summary.”, “Write the text of the post.”, “Wait until the photos are uploaded.”, “The image cannot be larger than 15 MB.”, “Choose a JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF or GIF photo.”</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>

    <HelpTopicSection Id="news-formatting">
        <p>The text of a post is formatted with the toolbar buttons above the field — like in an ordinary word processor. Keyboard shortcuts: <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>B</kbd> — bold, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>I</kbd> — italic, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>U</kbd> — underline, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Z</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Z</kbd> — undo / redo.</p>
        <div class="help-table-wrap">
            <table class="help-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Button</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>¶, H2, H3, H4</td><td>Normal text, heading, subheading, small heading</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>B, I, U, S, &lt;/&gt;</td><td>Bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, code</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Lists, quote, divider</td><td>Bulleted and numbered lists, a highlighted quote, a horizontal line</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Alignment</td><td>Left, center, right (for paragraphs and headings)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Link</td><td>Select text, click <span class="help-ui">Link</span>, enter the address and click <span class="help-ui">Apply</span>. http(s), mailto:, tel: and internal links are allowed; external links open in a new tab</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Table</td><td>Inserts a 3×3 table with a header row. While the cursor is in the table, buttons appear to add a row or a column, remove a row or a column, or delete the table</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Photo in the text</td><td>One or several photos across the width of the text</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Photo gallery</td><td>Several photos as tiles; readers open them full screen and browse. If the cursor is in a gallery, new photos are added to it</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Photos.</strong> JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF and GIF up to 15 MB are supported. Photos can also be pasted from the clipboard (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>) or dragged into the text. Each photo is uploaded to the server right away and optimized: reduced to 1600 pixels, compressed to AVIF within 10–100 KB, its metadata (including location) removed. Galleries also get thumbnails. A photo removed from the text is deleted when the post is saved.</p>
        <p>For security, the server keeps only this markup: scripts, embedded pages, images from other sites and arbitrary styles are removed. Posts written earlier in Markdown are shown as before and are saved in the new format after the first edit.</p>
    </HelpTopicSection>
</HelpChapterSection>
